        "faq_item_pYwK3f": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "name": "what is route TAB",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is Route Shipping Protection?",
            "answer": "<p><a href=\"https://shoppers.help.route.com/hc/en-us/articles/6026989008791-Shopper-FAQs\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"what is route?\"><strong>Route Shipping Protection</strong></a><strong> </strong>is an optional service you can add at checkout. It covers your order against loss, theft, or damage while in transit. <a href=\"https://claims.route.com/\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"file a claim\"><strong>Claims</strong></a> are handled directly by Route, not Light Provisions.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_JCGrTe": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "name": "how to file claim TAB",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How to file a claim?",
            "answer": "<p><strong>1. Find Your Order Info</strong><br/><br/>Have your order number, email, and shipping address ready.</p><p><br/><strong>2. Go to Route’s Claim Portal</strong><br/><br/>Visit <a href=\"https://claims.route.com/\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://claims.route.com/\"><strong>https://claims.route.com/</strong></a> and input your order number and email address.<br/></p><p><br/><strong>3. Submit Your Claim</strong><br/><br/>Fill in your order information, describe the issue (lost, stolen, or damaged), and upload any required photos (especially for damage claims).<br/></p><p><br/><strong>4. Wait for Route’s Review</strong><br/><br/>Route will review the claim according to its coverage terms and may issue a replacement or refund. For some claims, Route may also require identity verification, including a government-issued ID and selfie, to help prevent fraudulent claims.<br/></p><p><strong>Need help?</strong><br/><br/>If you have questions about Route’s process, email <a><strong>support@route.com</strong></a>. If your issue is about product quality or a packing error, contact us instead.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_dyjWWi": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "name": "why pay extra TAB",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Doesn’t shipping insurance already come with most orders? Why should I pay extra?",
            "answer": "<p>Most carriers include a limited amount of default insurance, but in practice, that coverage often applies only to certain situations and can be difficult to claim successfully.</p><p>If a package is marked delivered but goes missing, is stolen, or ends up at the wrong address, claims through USPS or UPS are frequently delayed, denied, or unresolved. Carrier investigations can also take weeks with no guaranteed outcome.</p><p>Route exists to cover the gaps carriers often do not. Claims are handled directly through Route, which usually means faster replacements or refunds without long back-and-forth investigations.</p><p>Route also acts as a neutral third party, helping keep the claims process fair and consistent for both customers and small businesses. For a lean business like ours, it also allows shipping issues to be resolved much faster than traditional carrier claim systems.</p><p><strong>We do not profit from Route coverage. The protection fee paid at checkout is passed directly to Route.</strong></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_NVJnzY": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "name": "scam TAB",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is Route a scam? Why should I have to pay for shipping protection?",
            "answer": "<p>We understand it can feel unusual to pay extra for shipping protection, especially when it is added at checkout by default. Route is a legitimate third-party company that provides optional coverage for packages that are lost, stolen, or damaged in transit. <strong>It can always be removed at checkout if you prefer not to use it.</strong></p><p>Most shipping issues happen after a carrier takes possession of a package. Resolving those issues directly through USPS or UPS can involve delays, documentation requests, and uncertain outcomes. Route exists to handle that process more quickly and independently.</p><p>When Route is selected at checkout, claims are handled directly through Route, which often leads to faster replacements or refunds without long carrier investigations or back-and-forth emails.</p><p>Many larger companies often build these costs into their product pricing. As a small business, offering optional shipping protection helps us keep pricing fair while still giving customers an easy way to protect their orders.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_FbAT8Q": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "name": "itnernational TAB",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does Route cover international shipments?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, Route covers both domestic and international shipments (except restricted countries). We strongly recommend it for international orders due to higher risk of loss or delay.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_fLcNqd": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "name": "how long TAB",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long do I have to file a claim?",
            "answer": "<ul><li>Packages marked “delivered”: file between 5–30 days after delivery.</li><li>Packages presumed lost: file after 7 days (domestic) or 20 days (international) but before 30 days from the last tracking checkpoint.</li></ul><p><strong>Please note that some claims may also require identity verification through Route before a refund or replacement is approved.</strong></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_XAxHN3": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "name": "local / in person TAB",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does Route cover local delivery or in-person pickup?",
            "answer": "<p>No. Route only applies to shipments sent via USPS, UPS, FedEx, or DHL.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
